+
+I basically commented-out entirely the "chance of evacuating code" and any "this unit type/unitai should evacuate but not this one" (paraphrased xd but anyways etc), which means that now if city is doomed, we always evacuate ALL land units, which is the best move since city is doomed anyway, why split our troops instead of rather regrouping to core cities and possibly coming back later in the game in this game i mean but anyways etc.
+
+Results are seemingly extremely good!!! Now (see existing screenshots between 213 and 217 anyways etc) our 11 unit stack successfully evacuates the city, and julius caesar ai captures it without blood xd (i think he lost 1 unit before that, still very bad trade to fight it there for us i mean in this case i mean but anyways etc). From there, i continued to autoplay it, and our AI makes a comeback in the game, eventually taking back the city with a strong position. Our AI could do it even after losing the stack (i assume due to julius caesar AI becoming weaker i guess although i didn't check lot), but now that it kept its stack, it seems like the comeback is very strong later in the game (turns 150-160 more or less although i didn't show here the screenshots so you have to believe me or see link of the forum possibly if i post it there rather but anyways etc), and game was actually winnable. I mean i had a great position overall and handling if not for this war carelessness, but it's impressive our AI could do it which i am very happy of it i may say but anyways etc.
